  ✔ OpenViking outage uses a durable outbox and recovers when back online (0.321167ms)
  ✔ reviewer isolation: brief contains only allowed content, never private history (0.181875ms)
✔ platform recovery + isolation (6.226167ms)
▶ CatalogRecoveryProbe: authenticated model listing
  ✔ is healthy only when the gateway lists the mission's model with capacity (26.296375ms)
  ✔ without the client token the gateway refuses, so the probe is not healthy (3.972625ms)
  ✔ an unresolvable target is reported as non-authoritative, never as a recovery (0.108209ms)
  ✔ resolves base URL, key and model from the worker's own ModelRuntime (15.227917ms)
✔ CatalogRecoveryProbe: authenticated model listing (46.486542ms)
▶ HttpRecoveryProbe (PI_GATEWAY_HEALTH_URL override)
  ✔ counts an InferWeave /healthz answer as reachable even when it says degraded (4.579791ms)
✔ HttpRecoveryProbe (PI_GATEWAY_HEALTH_URL override) (4.722042ms)
▶ RemoteHttpTransport (spec 12, Phase 2-lite)
  ✔ attaches an outbound channel and round-trips a heartbeat (325.329459ms)
  ✔ answers run_task with an honest not-yet-wired stub (305.922292ms)
  ✔ marks a worker recovering when the agent disconnects (202.271708ms)
✔ RemoteHttpTransport (spec 12, Phase 2-lite) (834.559042ms)
▶ repair loop (#182)
  ✖ sends three blocking findings to exactly one repair task naming all three (190.595542ms)
  ✖ records a high missing_tests finding without blocking completion (152.179792ms)
  ✖ retries a failed merge deterministically before creating any LLM repair task (140.881666ms)
  ✖ repairs a request_changes verdict whose findings are only non-blocking instead of dead-ending (172.424666ms)
  ✔ does not complete on an approve verdict that carries an open high correctness defect (282.431167ms)
  ✖ re-sends only the finding the next review still reports, without a duplicate row (132.927125ms)
  ✖ stops naming the preserved work once the deterministic merge budget is spent (128.117834ms)
  ✖ turns an integration whose checks ran and failed into a code-repair contract (136.344375ms)
  ✖ builds the contract task on the current candidate and carries the acceptance ids (170.820292ms)
✖ repair loop (#182) (1508.211917ms)
✔ interactive path: the installed wrapper sends a reduced COPY and learns the advertised cap (101.601542ms)
✔ interactive path: newest content over budget fails fast, never reaching the gateway (13.704375ms)
✔ interactive path: a gateway 413 lowers the learned cap, re-fits, and resends exactly once (79.9565ms)
✔ interactive path: a second 413 is final, explained, and not retried again (77.366292ms)
✔ interactive path: a 413 on a body under 1 MiB teaches nothing and is not resent (9.689375ms)
✔ compaction: summarization calls go through the same guarded streamSimple (59.295417ms)
✔ worker path: PiWorkerExecutor's runtime is guarded the same way (72.361417ms)
▶ (a) interrupted stream → same-model retry → mission continues
  ✔ retries the SAME model after an SSE stream ends without finish_reason; request 2 succeeds (6.853334ms)
  ✔ does NOT bubble an interrupted stream out of the invocation (worker stays alive through the wait) (1.602083ms)
✔ (a) interrupted stream → same-model retry → mission continues (9.329958ms)
▶ (b) no_workers → qwen temporarily penalized, catalog refreshed, DeepSeek selected
  ✔ falls back to the comparable model when the original has no workers (1.831541ms)
  ✔ never selects a fallback that misses a hard envelope requirement (9.39375ms)
✔ (b) no_workers → qwen temporarily penalized, catalog refreshed, DeepSeek selected (11.454208ms)
▶ (c) 429 reason=queue_timeout Retry-After=120 → wait >= 120s, same model retained
  ✔ honours the server wait exactly and never model-switches on a queue timeout (29.023791ms)
✔ (c) 429 reason=queue_timeout Retry-After=120 → wait >= 120s, same model retained (29.188708ms)
▶ (d) model_activating retry_after_ms=90000 → wait >= 90s, no premature fallback
  ✔ waits out activation and serves the same model when it activates in time (2.994625ms)
  ✔ falls back only after activation exceeds the configured threshold (1.523708ms)
✔ (d) model_activating retry_after_ms=90000 → wait >= 90s, no premature fallback (4.743083ms)
▶ (e) all models unavailable → durable capacity wait, scheduler continues, auto-resume
  ✔ parks the mission durably, keeps probing, and resumes the SAME request when capacity appears (0.979959ms)
✔ (e) all models unavailable → durable capacity wait, scheduler continues, auto-resume (1.074334ms)
▶ (f) edit executed, then stream disconnects → retry does NOT re-execute the edit
  ✔ injects concise idempotency evidence into the retried request and records the partial generation (0.6525ms)
  ✔ the retried request is the SAME logical request (mission state preserved) (0.693125ms)
✔ (f) edit executed, then stream disconnects → retry does NOT re-execute the edit (1.457166ms)
▶ live seam: gateway saturation is waited out on the SAME model (§32)
  ✔ honours Retry-After exactly, never switches model, and completes (57.736583ms)
✔ live seam: gateway saturation is waited out on the SAME model (§32) (58.62475ms)
▶ live seam: model-scoped no_workers falls back by capability (§31)
  ✔ penalises the model, refreshes the catalog and serves the comparable model (36.699125ms)
  ✔ never falls back for a gateway-scoped outage (34.118042ms)
✔ live seam: model-scoped no_workers falls back by capability (§31) (71.084292ms)
▶ live seam: interrupted stream after output (§30)
  ✔ records the incomplete generation and never replays committed output (13.222792ms)
✔ live seam: interrupted stream after output (§30) (13.364375ms)
▶ live seam: every model unavailable parks the mission (§34)
  ✔ parks WAITING_FOR_INFERENCE_CAPACITY, keeps probing and resumes (77.6235ms)
✔ live seam: every model unavailable parks the mission (§34) (77.800541ms)
▶ live seam: idempotency evidence for executed tool calls (§6)
  ✔ lists already-executed actions in the retried request without replaying them (36.662834ms)
✔ live seam: idempotency evidence for executed tool calls (§6) (36.871791ms)
▶ live seam: policy defaults (§19/§21)
  ✔ keeps interactive fallback off unless explicitly opted in (53.520708ms)
✔ live seam: policy defaults (§19/§21) (53.668709ms)
▶ re-arm of an already-wrapped runtime (spec §23 production arming)
  ✔ merges late-arriving registry/scheduler/status into the live install (8.191459ms)
  ✔ the wrapper reads the re-armed options per call (17764.925334ms)
✔ re-arm of an already-wrapped runtime (spec §23 production arming) (17774.393875ms)
▶ circuit-breaker gating of fallback selection (spec §13, FINDING-e63OXY)
  ✔ an OPEN breaker blocks same-model retry, excludes the model from fallback, and stays live (4.688083ms)
✔ circuit-breaker gating of fallback selection (spec §13, FINDING-e63OXY) (5.227125ms)
▶ interactive classifyAttempt (spec §21/§26, FINDING-XXHroG)
  ✔ unified verdicts with fallback forced off, even when a registry exists (1.323958ms)
✔ interactive classifyAttempt (spec §21/§26, FINDING-XXHroG) (1.440625ms)
▶ MissionCapacityScheduler (production WAITING_FOR_INFERENCE_CAPACITY)
  ✔ capacity query: penalized models and OPEN breakers are excluded (1.312208ms)
  ✔ no registry → no capacity (fail closed) (0.122542ms)
  ✔ park/resumed drive the guarded mission transition hook (0.450541ms)
✔ MissionCapacityScheduler (production WAITING_FOR_INFERENCE_CAPACITY) (2.050125ms)
▶ durable WAITING_FOR_INFERENCE_CAPACITY park (spec §20/§21)
  ✔ park persists as the real mission state and survives a restart (30.883083ms)
✔ durable WAITING_FOR_INFERENCE_CAPACITY park (spec §20/§21) (31.048417ms)
